    "body": "> They are different functions, see the spec [here](https://streams.spec.whatwg.org/#rs-cancel) and [here](https://streams.spec.whatwg.org/#default-reader-cancel). They have different preconditions, but they have the same effect (calling the abstract operation [ReadableStreamCancel](https://streams.spec.whatwg.org/#readable-stream-cancel)).\r\n\r\n\r\nDoes it mean, that the better/proper/primary/shorter cancellation route is:\r\n```javascript\r\nreader.releaseLock();\r\nstream.cancel();\r\n```\r\n\r\nAlso, does the \"loss of interest\" signaling means that i shall not do:\r\n```javascript\r\nreader = stream.getReader();\r\n```\r\n..anymore, and i should recreate a stream?\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n",
